(b) An antibody molecule is drawn as a Y-shaped structure made of four polypeptide chains, \(\text{H}_2\text{L}_2\). The labels (any four):
- **two heavy chains**, the two long chains forming the stem and the inner part of the arms;
- **two light chains**, the two short chains on the outer side of the arms;
- **antigen binding sites**, at the tips of the two arms (the N-terminal ends of the chains);
- **disulphide bonds**, holding each light chain to a heavy chain and the two heavy chains together;
- the **C-terminal ends** of the heavy chains at the base of the stem.

